Aligned with SWIP-74 rev 8 (ethersphere/SWIPs#111, SWIPs/swip-74.md). Still open:

1. Client backoff: a peer whose join was refused or whose stream was reset MUST back off
   (randomised exponential, 1s-30s, full jitter) before rejoining. Join is one-shot; the
   API websocket closes instead of retrying, so a reconnecting client owns the backoff.
2. Spec open points (?) follow the draft as written: the kind byte in the service prefix,
   streams per peer per cohort = 2, claim deadline = 30s.
3. Per-cohort counters are exposed via Service.Counters; there is no API endpoint for them
   yet (prometheus carries the aggregate per outcome).
4. Conformance 12 (interop with a full SWIP-60 broker) is untestable until SWIP-60 exists.
